# worktree-audit.sh, the upstream script the port changes most, and every change to it is code
# rather than prose, so a unified diff is the right layer for all of it.
#
# The changes, all of them code:
#   - read the omp session store instead of Cursor's per-project transcript directory, resolved
#     the way omp resolves it: an explicit PI_CODING_AGENT_SESSION_DIR is the transcript
#     directory itself with no cwd bucket; otherwise the profile (OMP_PROFILE, PI_PROFILE),
#     PI_CONFIG_DIR, PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR and an existing XDG_DATA_HOME/omp pick the root, and
#     each worktree's bucket is omp's encoding of its canonical path (-tmp-<rel> under the temp
#     root, checked first, -<rel> under home, --<abs>-- otherwise, / \ : mapped to -)
#   - scan only the buckets of this repo's worktrees, never the whole store, with grep -F, so
#     ripgrep is not required and a path with [ or spaces matches literally
#   - scan each linked worktree's subdirectory buckets too, found by the bucket-name prefix, since
#     omp files a session started in <worktree>/src under that cwd's own bucket
#   - scan those buckets in every store on disk, not only the one the audit's environment names:
#     the default agent dir, each profile's, PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR, and the XDG data and state
#     roots, so a session launched with --profile still counts
#   - read each store's custom-session-files, where omp lists the absolute path of every
#     transcript written outside the bucket store (--session-dir, PI_CODING_AGENT_SESSION_DIR,
#     --resume of a moved file), and scan those transcripts and their subagent directories,
#     skipping the bucket transcripts omp also lists under a symlinked home, which the bucket
#     scan already bounds to this repo's worktrees
#   - fail closed: a store that cannot be found or read, or an index that cannot be read, makes
#     LAST_CHAT "?" and holds the row at verify-recent-chat, the bucket
#     playbooks/worktree-cleanup.md already names, never `safe`
#   - fail closed the same way when a .env file omp reads (each worktree's, the agent dir's, the
#     config root's, home's) sets a key that moves the store, OMP_ spellings included, rather
#     than replaying omp's .env loader
#   - stat each matched transcript on its own through upstream's GNU/BSD probe, so a path with
#     spaces survives and a stat failure fails closed instead of dropping out of an xargs pipe
#   - keep the PR list in memory, so the audit writes no scratch file at all, inside the repo or
#     out of it
#   - parse `git worktree list` records by stripping the record prefix, so a path containing
#     spaces survives, and report a lock reason in its own LOCKED column
#   - record an unreadable worktree in a new INSPECT column and bucket it hold-error, rather
#     than letting a failed rev-parse read as a clean tree, and never mark a locked worktree
#     `safe`
#   - print all eleven header columns on every row
#   - lowercase the Origin PR state too, so upstream's */open|*/draft match holds for both CLIs
#   - carry upstream PR cursor/plugins#770 (#459 on #492) ahead of its merge: untracked and
#     ignored files count as wip, a closed but unmerged PR is no longer `safe`, the PR whose
#     headRefOid is HEAD wins over another PR on the same branch name, and commits that exist
#     nowhere else bucket as hold-unpushed
#
# Upstream's -b/--base flag, its origin/HEAD default, its Origin-first PR fetch with the gh
# fallback, its GNU/BSD stat and date probe, its LAST_CHAT column, and its verify-recent-chat
# bucket are all kept exactly as written.
#
# Authored against post-rules text. rules.sed runs first and rewrites the Cursor path in the
# comment this patch deletes, so a hunk quoting the raw upstream comment would not apply.
# omp-port/test-worktree-audit.sh is the offline regression test for every change above.
